<p>&#8230; grasping at straws here. I guess it comes with the territory when reading SCPs and filling the gaps. It might just be a self sustaining mining station that was meant as the perfect replacement for human miners (a difficult, dangerous and generally terrible job) and somehow stopped working as intended, becoming a sort-of-sentient clone factory that only cares about its self-preservation. I wouldn't be surprised if, underneath -A there was a bunch of tubes that processed the obtained material and dumped it back to the tunnels in ore form, thus perpetuating the process, because -A decided that, if it run out if ore to extract, its existence would bear no meaning.</p>
<p>Dammit, I'm doing it again. Sorry. : (</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Anyways, a great story. : )</p>

